1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,248
Formulas like distance equals rate times
time are equations with several letters.

2
00:00:05,698 --> 00:00:10,306
In this lesson, we'll rearrange formulas
to solve for whichever letter we need.

3
00:00:11,433 --> 00:00:15,700
An equation with more than one variable is
called a literal equation.

4
00:00:16,150 --> 00:00:20,139
To solve for one letter, treat every other
letter as if it were a number.

5
00:00:20,589 --> 00:00:25,594
Then use the same moves as always: do the
same thing to both sides, and undo

6
00:00:25,594 --> 00:00:27,437
operations in reverse order.

7
00:00:28,567 --> 00:00:30,849
Let's solve d equals r t for t.

8
00:00:31,299 --> 00:00:37,742
t is multiplied by r, so divide both sides
by r. That gives t equals d over r.

9
00:00:38,192 --> 00:00:43,483
Now if you drive a hundred fifty miles at
fifty miles per hour, t equals a hundred

10
00:00:43,483 --> 00:00:46,000
fifty over fifty, which is three hours.

11
00:00:47,133 --> 00:00:53,048
Compare these two equations side by side.
Two x plus three equals eleven, and a x

12
00:00:53,048 --> 00:00:54,216
plus b equals c.

13
00:00:54,666 --> 00:01:00,554
In both, subtract the constant first. Two
x equals eight, and a x equals c minus b.

14
00:01:01,004 --> 00:01:07,148
Then divide by the coefficient. x equals
four, and x equals c minus b, all over a.

15
00:01:07,598 --> 00:01:12,179
The steps are identical. The only
difference is that the answer on the right

16
00:01:12,179 --> 00:01:13,806
is a formula, not a number.

17
00:01:14,933 --> 00:01:20,971
The perimeter of a rectangle is P equals
two l plus two w. Let's solve for w.

18
00:01:21,421 --> 00:01:26,178
Subtract two l from both sides: P minus
two l equals two w.

19
00:01:26,628 --> 00:01:31,577
Divide both sides by two: w equals P minus
two l, all over two.

20
00:01:32,700 --> 00:01:38,088
Here's a famous one. Fahrenheit equals
nine fifths Celsius plus thirty-two. Let's

21
00:01:38,088 --> 00:01:38,887
solve for C.

22
00:01:39,337 --> 00:01:43,369
Subtract thirty-two: F minus thirty-two
equals nine fifths C.

23
00:01:43,819 --> 00:01:49,657
Multiply both sides by five ninths, the
reciprocal of nine fifths. C equals five

24
00:01:49,657 --> 00:01:53,013
ninths, times the quantity F minus
thirty-two.

25
00:01:53,463 --> 00:01:58,786
Check with boiling water. F is two hundred
twelve. Two twelve minus thirty-two is a

26
00:01:58,786 --> 00:02:03,532
hundred eighty, and five ninths of a
hundred eighty is one hundred degrees

27
00:02:03,532 --> 00:02:04,045
Celsius.

28
00:02:05,167 --> 00:02:10,372
Your turn. The area of a triangle is A
equals one half b h. Solve for h.

29
00:02:10,822 --> 00:02:12,273
Pause the video and try it.

30
00:02:12,723 --> 00:02:15,987
Multiply both sides by two: two A equals b
h.

31
00:02:16,437 --> 00:02:19,850
Divide both sides by b: h equals two A
over b.

32
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Next time, we'll use equations to solve
ratio, proportion and percent problems. If

33
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:25,736
Here's a worked example of rearranging a
formula you'll see in geometry.

34
00:02:27,167 --> 00:02:32,720
The area of a trapezoid is A equals one
half h times the quantity b one plus b

35
00:02:32,720 --> 00:02:38,557
two. Solve for b one, then find b one when
the area is sixty, the height is eight,

36
00:02:38,557 --> 00:02:39,839
and b two is nine.

37
00:02:40,967 --> 00:02:44,273
First, clear the fraction. Multiply both
sides by two.

38
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:47,384
Next, divide both sides by h.

39
00:02:48,533 --> 00:02:52,779
Finally, subtract b two from both sides.
Now b one is alone.

40
00:02:53,900 --> 00:02:57,399
Now substitute: two times sixty, over
eight, minus nine.

41
00:02:58,533 --> 00:03:02,864
One hundred twenty over eight is fifteen,
and fifteen minus nine is six.

42
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:09,376
So b one equals two A over h, minus b two.
With these numbers, b one is six.

43
00:03:10,500 --> 00:03:15,509
Watch out. Undo the operations in reverse
order, just like a normal equation. Treat

44
00:03:15,509 --> 00:03:20,579
the other letters as if they were numbers.
And it's usually cleaner to solve for the

45
00:03:20,579 --> 00:03:22,511
variable first, then substitute.

46
00:03:23,633 --> 00:03:30,570
Your turn. Solve P equals two l plus two w
for w, then find w when P is forty six and

47
00:03:30,570 --> 00:03:33,916
l is fifteen. Pause the video and try it.

48
00:03:38,433 --> 00:03:44,611
Subtract two l and divide by two: w equals
P minus two l, over two. That's forty six

49
00:03:44,611 --> 00:03:47,479
minus thirty, over two, which is eight.

50
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:53,485
Ratios, proportions and percents show up
everywhere, from recipes to shopping.

51
00:03:53,935 --> 00:03:58,486
In this lesson, we'll turn them into
equations, and solve them with one simple

52
00:03:58,486 --> 00:03:58,778
tool.

53
00:03:59,900 --> 00:04:05,262
A ratio compares two quantities. If a
class has twelve boys and fifteen girls,

54
00:04:05,262 --> 00:04:08,561
the ratio of boys to girls is twelve to
fifteen.

55
00:04:09,011 --> 00:04:11,529
You can write it with a colon, or as a
fraction.

56
00:04:11,979 --> 00:04:17,108
Like fractions, ratios can be simplified.
Divide both by three, and twelve to

57
00:04:17,108 --> 00:04:19,040
fifteen becomes four to five.

58
00:04:20,167 --> 00:04:25,784
A proportion says two ratios are equal.
For example, x over six equals ten over

59
00:04:25,784 --> 00:04:26,353
fifteen.

60
00:04:26,803 --> 00:04:31,497
To solve it, cross-multiply. Fifteen times
x equals six times ten.

61
00:04:31,947 --> 00:04:36,768
That's fifteen x equals sixty. Divide by
fifteen, and x equals four.

62
00:04:37,218 --> 00:04:42,402
Cross-multiplying works because it's the
same as multiplying both sides by both

63
00:04:42,402 --> 00:04:43,255
denominators.

64
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:49,264
Here's a real problem. Three notebooks
cost seven dollars fifty. How much do

65
00:04:49,264 --> 00:04:50,608
eight notebooks cost?

66
00:04:51,058 --> 00:04:56,242
Set up matching ratios of notebooks to
dollars: three over seven fifty equals

67
00:04:56,242 --> 00:04:57,117
eight over x.

68
00:04:57,567 --> 00:05:03,514
Cross-multiply: three x equals sixty. So x
equals twenty. Eight notebooks cost twenty

69
00:05:03,514 --> 00:05:04,073
dollars.

70
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:10,921
A percent is a ratio out of one hundred.
So part over whole equals percent over one

71
00:05:10,921 --> 00:05:11,472
hundred.

72
00:05:11,922 --> 00:05:16,477
What is thirty percent of eighty? Write p
over eighty equals thirty over one

73
00:05:16,477 --> 00:05:16,957
hundred.

74
00:05:17,407 --> 00:05:22,483
Cross-multiply: one hundred p equals two
thousand four hundred. So p equals

75
00:05:22,483 --> 00:05:23,295
twenty-four.

76
00:05:23,745 --> 00:05:29,035
Or, as a shortcut, multiply zero point
three zero by eighty. Same answer.

77
00:05:30,167 --> 00:05:34,796
The same setup finds a missing whole.
Eighteen is forty-five percent of what

78
00:05:34,796 --> 00:05:35,223
number?

79
00:05:35,673 --> 00:05:39,257
Eighteen over w equals forty-five over one
hundred.

80
00:05:39,707 --> 00:05:45,893
Cross-multiply: forty-five w equals one
thousand eight hundred. So w equals forty.

81
00:05:47,033 --> 00:05:50,681
For percent change, divide the change by
the original amount.

82
00:05:51,131 --> 00:05:56,059
A price goes from fifty dollars to sixty
dollars. The change is ten dollars.

83
00:05:56,509 --> 00:06:00,733
Ten over fifty is zero point two, which is
a twenty percent increase.

84
00:06:01,867 --> 00:06:04,384
Your turn. Twelve is what percent of
forty-eight?

85
00:06:04,834 --> 00:06:06,285
Pause the video and try it.

86
00:06:06,735 --> 00:06:10,233
Set up twelve over forty-eight equals p
over one hundred.

87
00:06:10,683 --> 00:06:15,802
Cross-multiply: forty-eight p equals one
thousand two hundred. So p equals

88
00:06:15,802 --> 00:06:19,814
twenty-five. Twelve is twenty-five percent
of forty-eight.

89
00:06:20,933 --> 00:06:23,792
Let's work through a percent problem that
has two steps.

90
00:06:26,033 --> 00:06:31,266
A jacket costs eighty dollars. It's marked
down twenty five percent, then six percent

91
00:06:31,266 --> 00:06:35,944
sales tax is added. What's the final
price, and what percent of the original

92
00:06:35,944 --> 00:06:36,806
price is that?

93
00:06:36,933 --> 00:06:42,114
First find the discount. Twenty five
percent of eighty is twenty dollars.

94
00:06:43,233 --> 00:06:46,817
So the sale price is eighty minus twenty,
or sixty dollars.

95
00:06:47,966 --> 00:06:53,176
The tax is charged on the sale price, not
the original. Six percent of sixty is

96
00:06:53,176 --> 00:06:54,494
three dollars sixty.

97
00:06:55,633 --> 00:07:00,966
The final price is sixty plus three sixty,
or sixty three dollars and sixty cents.

98
00:07:02,100 --> 00:07:08,073
To compare with the original, divide part
by whole. Sixty three sixty over eighty is

99
00:07:08,073 --> 00:07:12,553
zero point seven nine five, or seventy
nine point five percent.

100
00:07:13,700 --> 00:07:19,057
The final price is sixty three dollars and
sixty cents, which is seventy nine point

101
00:07:19,057 --> 00:07:21,316
five percent of the original price.

102
00:07:22,433 --> 00:07:27,467
Watch out. The tax applies to the sale
price. You can't just combine minus twenty

103
00:07:27,467 --> 00:07:32,066
five and plus six into minus nineteen
percent. A quick way is multipliers:

104
00:07:32,066 --> 00:07:36,976
twenty five percent off means times zero
point seven five, and six percent more

105
00:07:36,976 --> 00:07:38,902
means times one point zero six.

106
00:07:40,033 --> 00:07:44,772
Your turn. A one hundred twenty dollar
game is thirty percent off, then eight

107
00:07:44,772 --> 00:07:49,142
percent tax is added. Find the final
price. Pause the video and try it.

108
00:07:53,666 --> 00:07:58,883
One hundred twenty times zero point seven
is eighty four. Eighty four times one

109
00:07:58,883 --> 00:08:02,648
point zero eight is ninety dollars and
seventy two cents.

110
00:08:03,766 --> 00:08:06,625
Word problems are where equations become
useful.

111
00:08:07,075 --> 00:08:11,555
In this lesson, we'll turn stories into
equations, using a four-step plan.

112
00:08:12,699 --> 00:08:17,073
Step one: define a variable. Write down
exactly what x stands for.

113
00:08:17,523 --> 00:08:20,211
Step two: translate the words into an
equation.

114
00:08:20,661 --> 00:08:22,346
Step three: solve the equation.

115
00:08:22,796 --> 00:08:26,508
Step four: answer the question in words,
and check that it makes sense.

116
00:08:27,633 --> 00:08:31,622
The sum of three consecutive integers is
seventy-two. What are they?

117
00:08:32,072 --> 00:08:36,595
Let n be the smallest. Then the next two
are n plus one and n plus two.

118
00:08:37,045 --> 00:08:42,711
So n plus n plus one plus n plus two
equals seventy-two. That's three n plus

119
00:08:42,711 --> 00:08:44,575
three equals seventy-two.

120
00:08:45,025 --> 00:08:50,594
Subtract three: three n equals sixty-nine.
So n equals twenty-three. The integers are

121
00:08:50,594 --> 00:08:53,345
twenty-three, twenty-four and twenty-five.

122
00:08:54,466 --> 00:08:59,949
A phone plan costs twenty dollars a month,
plus ten cents per text. One month's bill

123
00:08:59,949 --> 00:09:03,213
was thirty-five dollars. How many texts
were sent?

124
00:09:03,663 --> 00:09:09,401
Let t be the number of texts. Then twenty
plus zero point one t equals thirty-five.

125
00:09:09,851 --> 00:09:15,509
Subtract twenty: zero point one t equals
fifteen. Divide by zero point one: t

126
00:09:15,509 --> 00:09:17,787
equals one hundred fifty texts.

127
00:09:18,933 --> 00:09:24,271
Gym A charges a forty dollar joining fee
plus twenty-five dollars a month. Gym B

128
00:09:24,271 --> 00:09:29,343
charges thirty-five dollars a month with
no fee. When do they cost the same?

129
00:09:29,793 --> 00:09:35,367
Let m be the number of months. Gym A costs
forty plus twenty-five m. Gym B costs

130
00:09:35,367 --> 00:09:36,343
thirty-five m.

131
00:09:36,793 --> 00:09:40,974
Set them equal: forty plus twenty-five m
equals thirty-five m.

132
00:09:41,424 --> 00:09:47,545
Subtract twenty-five m: forty equals ten
m. So m equals four. After four months,

133
00:09:47,545 --> 00:09:50,683
both gyms cost one hundred forty dollars.

134
00:09:51,833 --> 00:09:57,312
A rectangle has a perimeter of fifty-four
centimeters. Its length is three more than

135
00:09:57,312 --> 00:09:59,726
twice its width. Find its dimensions.

136
00:10:00,176 --> 00:10:03,952
Let w be the width. Then the length is two
w plus three.

137
00:10:04,402 --> 00:10:10,337
Perimeter is two lengths plus two widths:
two times the quantity two w plus three,

138
00:10:10,337 --> 00:10:12,509
plus two w, equals fifty-four.

139
00:10:12,959 --> 00:10:19,223
That simplifies to six w plus six equals
fifty-four. So six w equals forty-eight,

140
00:10:19,223 --> 00:10:23,476
and w equals eight. The length is nineteen
centimeters.

141
00:10:24,599 --> 00:10:29,371
Your turn. Maya has a hundred twenty
dollars and saves fifteen dollars a week.

142
00:10:29,371 --> 00:10:33,898
Leo has sixty dollars and saves
twenty-five dollars a week. After how many

143
00:10:33,898 --> 00:10:36,162
weeks will they have the same amount?

144
00:10:36,612 --> 00:10:38,063
Pause the video and try it.

145
00:10:38,513 --> 00:10:44,420
Let w be the number of weeks. One twenty
plus fifteen w equals sixty plus

146
00:10:44,420 --> 00:10:45,553
twenty-five w.

147
00:10:46,003 --> 00:10:52,817
Subtract fifteen w and sixty from both
sides: sixty equals ten w. So w equals

148
00:10:52,817 --> 00:10:53,171
six.

149
00:10:53,621 --> 00:10:57,333
Check: after six weeks, each of them has
two hundred ten dollars.

150
00:10:58,466 --> 00:11:01,901
Let's solve a classic motion word problem,
step by step.

151
00:11:03,566 --> 00:11:08,620
Two trains leave the same station at the
same time, going in opposite directions.

152
00:11:08,620 --> 00:11:13,861
One travels fifteen miles per hour faster
than the other. After three hours they are

153
00:11:13,861 --> 00:11:17,667
three hundred forty five miles apart. How
fast is each train?

154
00:11:18,799 --> 00:11:24,065
Define the variable. Let r be the slower
train's speed. Then the faster train goes

155
00:11:24,065 --> 00:11:25,029
r plus fifteen.

156
00:11:26,166 --> 00:11:31,062
Distance is rate times time. They move
apart, so the two distances add up to

157
00:11:31,062 --> 00:11:32,673
three hundred forty five.

158
00:11:33,799 --> 00:11:39,026
Distribute and combine: six r plus forty
five equals three hundred forty five.

159
00:11:40,166 --> 00:11:43,387
Subtract forty five: six r equals three
hundred.

160
00:11:44,533 --> 00:11:49,912
Divide by six. The slower train goes fifty
miles per hour, and the faster one goes

161
00:11:49,912 --> 00:11:50,634
sixty five.

162
00:11:51,766 --> 00:11:55,243
The trains travel at fifty and sixty five
miles per hour.

163
00:11:56,366 --> 00:12:01,150
Watch out. Always write what your variable
means. When objects move in opposite

164
00:12:01,150 --> 00:12:05,753
directions, their distances add. And
answer the actual question, with units.

165
00:12:06,899 --> 00:12:12,247
Your turn. Two cyclists ride in opposite
directions. One is four miles per hour

166
00:12:12,247 --> 00:12:17,866
faster. After two hours they are fifty six
miles apart. Find both speeds. Pause the

167
00:12:17,866 --> 00:12:19,017
video and try it.

168
00:12:23,566 --> 00:12:29,149
Two r plus two times r plus four equals
fifty six. So four r plus eight is fifty

169
00:12:29,149 --> 00:12:34,105
six, r is twelve, and the speeds are
twelve and sixteen miles per hour.

170
00:12:35,233 --> 00:12:40,656
Let's finish Unit Two with one realistic
problem that uses equations, formulas and

171
00:12:40,656 --> 00:12:41,846
percents together.

172
00:12:43,266 --> 00:12:47,776
A class trip costs four hundred fifty
dollars for the bus plus eighteen dollars

173
00:12:47,776 --> 00:12:52,115
per student for tickets. The school pays
forty percent of the total, and the

174
00:12:52,115 --> 00:12:56,624
students split the rest equally. If each
student pays fifteen dollars, how many

175
00:12:56,624 --> 00:12:57,709
students are going?

176
00:12:58,833 --> 00:13:04,103
Let n be the number of students. The total
cost is four hundred fifty plus eighteen

177
00:13:04,103 --> 00:13:04,230
n.

178
00:13:05,366 --> 00:13:09,804
The school pays forty percent, so the
students pay sixty percent of the total.

179
00:13:10,933 --> 00:13:16,901
That share is also fifteen dollars times n
students. So the equation is zero point

180
00:13:16,901 --> 00:13:19,594
six times the total equals fifteen n.

181
00:13:20,733 --> 00:13:26,485
Distribute: zero point six times four
fifty is two seventy, and zero point six

182
00:13:26,485 --> 00:13:29,288
times eighteen n is ten point eight n.

183
00:13:30,433 --> 00:13:35,288
Subtract ten point eight n from both
sides: two hundred seventy equals four

184
00:13:35,288 --> 00:13:36,065
point two n.

185
00:13:37,200 --> 00:13:42,475
Divide by four point two. n is about sixty
four point three. But students come in

186
00:13:42,475 --> 00:13:43,386
whole numbers.

187
00:13:44,533 --> 00:13:49,628
Check sixty four students. The total is
sixteen oh two, the students owe nine

188
00:13:49,628 --> 00:13:55,054
sixty one twenty, which is about fifteen
dollars and two cents each. Very close to

189
00:13:55,054 --> 00:13:55,584
fifteen.

190
00:13:56,733 --> 00:14:01,751
So about sixty four students are going.
With exactly sixty four, each pays about

191
00:14:01,751 --> 00:14:06,205
fifteen dollars and two cents, so the
fifteen dollar price was rounded.

192
00:14:07,333 --> 00:14:11,965
Watch out. If the school pays forty
percent, the students pay sixty. The key

193
00:14:11,965 --> 00:14:16,781
idea is one equation that describes the
same amount of money in two ways. And a

194
00:14:16,781 --> 00:14:21,840
real answer has to make sense, so round to
a whole number of students and check it.

195
00:14:22,966 --> 00:14:27,679
Your turn. A club rents a hall for three
hundred dollars plus twelve dollars per

196
00:14:27,679 --> 00:14:32,509
guest. A sponsor pays twenty five percent,
and each guest pays fourteen dollars of

197
00:14:32,509 --> 00:14:36,278
the rest. How many guests are there? Pause
the video and try it.

198
00:14:40,800 --> 00:14:46,117
Zero point seven five times the quantity
three hundred plus twelve g equals

199
00:14:46,117 --> 00:14:51,718
fourteen g. That's two twenty five plus
nine g equals fourteen g, so two twenty

200
00:14:51,718 --> 00:14:55,050
five equals five g, and g is forty five
guests.

